To perform such studies, a set of different tools is used. In particular:

a quantitative assessment of frequencies of trigger events is performed;

a semi-quantitative approach is used to rank trigger events, with help of a standardised Frequency-Consequence matrix;

a quantitative consequence analysis (smoke movement, user behaviour, etc.) is performed for a set of representative scenarios, selected in the above mentioned matrix, and using standardised source terms for fires. The analysis. to quantify the consequences of fires generally considers a combination of a model to assess smoke and temperature conditions in the tunnel with a model to assess self rescue of people.

4.4.2. Results of risk analysis and strategy of risk evaluation

The main results of the specific hazard investigation are generally summarised as follows:

the compliance with widely accepted practice of measures intended to reduce the probability of occurrence of accidents is assessed;

for  tunnels  in  operation  that  do  not  comply  with  the  French  2000-63 technical  instruction  and/or  the  EU  Directive,  an  assessment  of  the level of safety is performed aiming to evaluate whether deviations from standards are acceptable or not regarding safety;

